# Phase 1 package — evidence-only mixed-host live certification

## Intent

Run one persistent, fail-closed operator sequence. Before either host launches, prove a source reported as bundle `com.apple.Music` and backed by a live `/Music.app/Contents/MacOS/Music` process changes `playing` state and returns byte-for-byte to its canonical starting snapshot through two checkpointed `media-control` operations. Then launch both exact isolated hosts in returned regular Herdr panes and prove shared rendered state, controls in both directions, Pi reload continuity, normal exits and owned process cleanup, post-Pi OpenCode control, exact playback restoration, unchanged daemon identity, and disappearance of only the two owned peers. Baseline and final unrelated peer inventories are evidence context, not an equality assertion.

## Protected boundaries and operating constraints

- Preserve verified product commit `bd952919` (`fix(music): tolerate daemon hello reset window`), its parent `c78b5b93`, the current `test(release): verify full repository gate` Apnea working-copy change, and unrelated Apnea records. Artifact writes may resnapshot the mutable working-copy commit ID; validate description, ancestry, and diff rather than pinning that mutable ID.
