- A protected PID, command, socket tuple/owner/mode, or generation mismatch is a blocker, never permission to repair the shared runtime. An owned-host peer mismatch is also a blocker. Unrelated peer arrivals/departures are recorded as context and are not failures because unrelated clients may exit naturally.
