## Dependencies

- Approved deterministic/focused tests, packed-host smokes, literal `bun run check`, and protected-daemon evidence represented by preserved verified commits; this evidence-only phase does not rerun the full gate.
- `HERDR_ENV=1`, installed regular-pane Herdr controls, `jq`, `lsof`, `media-control`, Bun, and registry access.
- A real controllable Music.app source exposing `com.apple.Music` through `media-control`. An unchanged uncontrollable Music.app item may be rejected only after evidence; a changed candidate must be exactly restored or the phase stops.
- Protected daemon PID `45621`, command, socket tuple/ownership/mode, and generation remain healthy throughout. Unrelated peers may arrive or depart naturally and are context only.

## Non-goals

- Product/test/docs/config/manifest/lockfile changes or new commits.
- Re-running `bun run check` or substituting synthetic/RPC evidence for rendered hosts.
- Global OpenCode/Pi installation or configuration.
- Next/previous/seek/provider-switch testing.
- Daemon startup, restart, signaling, unlinking, discovery cleanup, replacement, or final idle shutdown.
- Signals, `ctrl+c`, OpenCode `/quit`, shortcut-encoded music control, floating panes, inferred IDs, or unrelated cleanup.
- Push, publication, release, or PR creation/update.
